# 11. SECURITY, PRIVACY AND ACADEMIC INTEGRITY

Implement sensible protections.

- Never expose private API keys in browser code.
- Use secure server-side functions or the platform's appropriate protected AI integration.
- Validate uploads and requests.
- Limit image sizes and processing duration.
- Prevent arbitrary code execution on the server.
- Do not run submitted code unless a properly isolated execution environment has been implemented.
- Do not send submissions to external services unnecessarily.
- Tell students when their work is processed by an external AI provider.
- Do not claim that submitted work is completely private unless the actual architecture supports that claim.
- Allow students to delete their saved drafts and review history.
- Do not present the AI's review as an official competition judge's verdict.

The app's academic-integrity promise is about not generating or correcting student solutions. Do not claim to detect plagiarism or guarantee that submitted work cannot be considered plagiarism.

